                // So we return invalid data error? Actually test: file with gzip content but no ext and -z gave invalid data. That suggests if extension not recognized, even though content is gzip, it will not decompress and will treat as plain, then later "invalid data" from literal missing newline? Wait that test was with -L -d, -f1 and file content gzip but no ext and -z, result was invalid data (because raw gzip bytes not newline terminated?).
                // So we treat as plain.
                return Ok(Box::new(BufReader::new(std::io::Cursor::new(raw_data))));
